body: "Issue: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/issues/228. The dispatch step polls until it can land the PR (7200 s with github.token, 2400 s with an app token, over 120/40 attempts). The caller CI it waits for needs runners from the same free-tier account pool: between 10:00Z and 12:00Z on 2026-11-09, 77 fleet runs queued while 8 ran; a scheduled sync sat in that step from 10:27Z, holding a runner while waiting for CI that could not start. An automation job must never wait in-job for work that competes for the same runner pool.\n\nPlan: dispatch caller CI, arm GitHub native auto-merge on the owned PR, report parked runs and exit. When auto-merge cannot be armed (GITHUB_TOKEN mode, no branch protection, disabled setting), print a notice with the reason; the next scheduled sync rebuilds and retries the PR. Persistent configuration problems require maintainer attention. Remove the whole polling class from both reusable workflows (sync and closeout), add timeout-minutes to every reusable job, add a contract test that fails on revert."
